swer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Point : Distance formula is covered under “Co-ordinate Geometry”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Mid-point formula, Straight Line : Forms of equations of straight lines : Slope-Point form, Two points form, Intercept form, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Mid-point formula; Straight Line : Forms of equations of straight lines : Slope-Point form; Two points form; Intercept form. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-IV problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Integration accumulates a quantity or represents area under a curve. Definite integrals have bounds and the result''s units follow from the integrand and variable.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Some particular integrals; Integration by substitution method; Integration by parts; Integration by partial fraction (for linear factors). State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-IV problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error