frigeration System. COP and TOR of refrigeration. Types of Primary Refrigerants: Ammonia, Halo Carbons (Freon of Different type), give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Methods of Refrigeration: (i) Ice Refrigeration, (ii) Evaporative Refrigeration, (iii) Vapor Refrigeration System. COP and TOR of refrigeration. Types of Primary Refrigerants: Ammonia, Halo Carbons (Freon of Different type).\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Different Temperature scale is included in “Measuring Devices”. Define its role, describe its main steps/components, relate it to Principle, Construction & Working of: Mercury in glass thermometer, Bi-metallic thermometer, pressure spring thermometer, give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Principle, Construction & Working of: Mercury in glass thermometer, Bi-metallic thermometer, pressure spring thermometer.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Function of relays and interlocks is included in “Control Valves, Control Loops & Control System”. Define its role, describe its main steps/components, relate it to Control loops: Temperature control, Pressure control, Flow control, Level control. Process control modes : P, give an application and a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Explain the concept and connect it to Control loops: Temperature control, Pressure control, Flow control, Level control. Process control modes : P.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical PLANT UTILIZATION AND INSTRUMENTATION task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and state one limitation or trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

