VALUES (460009382402011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Simple problems by direct use formula. Thermal Conductivity of solids in the context of “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Thermal conductivity. Steady state (S.S.) heat conduction through composite wall in the context of “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Shell and tube heat exchanger: (a) 1-1 Pass (b) 1-2 Pass (c) 2-4 Pass in the context of “Heat exchangers”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain liquids and gases. in the context of “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Thermal conductivity quantifies how readily a material conducts heat and appears in Fourier''s law.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Heat Transfer by Conduction.; Fourier s law of heat conduction with Concepts of (a) Heat transfer rate (b) Heat flux (c) T; Thermal conductivity. Steady state (S.S.) heat conduction through composite wall; S.S. heat conduction through composite cylinder up to three layers. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Conduction transfers thermal energy through a material and is commonly described using Fourier''s law.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Heat Transfer by Conduction.; Fourier s law of heat conduction with Concepts of (a) Heat transfer rate (b) Heat flux (c) T; S.S. heat conduction through composite cylinder up to three layers; S.S. heat conduction through composite sphere up to three layers. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A shell-and-tube exchanger transfers heat between fluids separated by tube walls; pass arrangement, fouling and flow configuration affect performance.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Heat exchangers; Types of heat exchanger; Double pipe heat exchanger (a) Counter current (b) Co-current; Plate type heat exchanger. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Heat exchangers”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Conduction transfers thermal energy through a material and is commonly described using Fourier''s law.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Heat Transfer by Conduction.; Fourier s law of heat conduction with Concepts of (a) Heat transfer rate (b) Heat flux (c) T; Thermal conductivity. Steady state (S.S.) heat conduction through composite wall; S.S. heat conduction through composite cylinder up to three layers. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

