VALUES (4600093824020111, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Classification of modes of heat transfer within “Introduction to Heat Transfer”. Explain the principles, justify your chosen method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Heat transfer in agitated vessels within “Heat exchangers”. Explain the principles, justify your chosen method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Definition of Heat Transfer and its importance in process industries within “Introduction to Heat Transfer”. Explain the principles, justify your chosen method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Fourier s law of heat conduction with Concepts of (a) Heat transfer rate (b) Heat flux (c) T within “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. Explain the principles, justify your chosen method, and state a verification check and one limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Classification of modes of heat transfer is listed under “Introduction to Heat Transfer” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Introduction to Heat Transfer, Definition of Heat Transfer and its importance in process industries, Differentiation of steady and unsteady state of heat transfer., and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Introduction to Heat Transfer; Definition of Heat Transfer and its importance in process industries; Differentiation of steady and unsteady state of heat transfer.. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Introduction to Heat Transfer”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A heat exchanger transfers energy between streams. The heat duty, temperature driving force, area, fouling and pressure drop affect design.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Heat exchangers; Types of heat exchanger; Double pipe heat exchanger (a) Counter current (b) Co-current; Shell and tube heat exchanger: (a) 1-1 Pass (b) 1-2 Pass (c) 2-4 Pass. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Heat exchangers”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Definition of Heat Transfer and its importance in process industries is listed under “Introduction to Heat Transfer” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Introduction to Heat Transfer, Classification of modes of heat transfer, Differentiation of steady and unsteady state of heat transfer., and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Introduction to Heat Transfer; Classification of modes of heat transfer; Differentiation of steady and unsteady state of heat transfer.. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Introduction to Heat Transfer”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Conduction transfers thermal energy through a material and is commonly described using Fourier''s law.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Heat Transfer by Conduction.; Thermal conductivity. Steady state (S.S.) heat conduction through composite wall; S.S. heat conduction through composite cylinder up to three layers; S.S. heat conduction through composite sphere up to three layers. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete PROCESS HEAT TRANSFER problem from “Heat Transfer by Conduction.”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

