VALUES (460009382401011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Importance of Mass Transfer Operation in the context of “Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Classification of Mass Transfer Operations in the context of “Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Statement of Fick s first law for diffusivity in the context of “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Steady state diffusion of following (a) Component A through non diffusing B (b) Equimolal co in the context of “Molecular Diffusion in Fluids”. Define it, state the key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Importance of Mass Transfer Operation is listed under “Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation, Classification of Mass Transfer Operations, Choice of separation method, Methods of conducting Mass Transfer Operations., and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation; Classification of Mass Transfer Operations; Choice of separation method; Methods of conducting Mass Transfer Operations.. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete UNIT OPERATION - III problem from “Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Classification of Mass Transfer Operations is listed under “Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation” in the syllabus. Define the concept, explain its role and main process/design steps, relate it to Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation, Importance of Mass Transfer Operation, Choice of separation method, Methods of conducting Mass Transfer Operations., and apply it to a chemical-engineering operation or equipment decision. State relevant variables or assumptions and describe a check for the result and a limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in a logical sequence and relate it to Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation; Importance of Mass Transfer Operation; Choice of separation method; Methods of conducting Mass Transfer Operations.. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units for calculations.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete UNIT OPERATION - III problem from “Introduction to Mass Transfer Operation”. State the objective, expected outcome and reason for choosing the method.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the process/design objective and note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm technical details against official teaching material."':